WEBVTT

00:09.009 --> 00:10.593
- [man groaning]
- [goons kicking]

00:17.767 --> 00:18.601
[Gun-woo grunts]

00:20.895 --> 00:23.023
- [Gun-woo grunting]
- [goon 1] huh?

00:23.106 --> 00:24.566
[uptempo instrumental music playing]

00:24.649 --> 00:26.359
[Jae-myeong] The fuck?
Who the hell are you?

00:27.902 --> 00:29.487
[breathes deeply]

00:35.785 --> 00:37.996
Come on. Come on, you son of a bitch.

00:38.621 --> 00:39.539
[Woo-jin] Asshole!

00:40.206 --> 00:41.624
[groans]

00:42.292 --> 00:43.376
[both panting]

00:43.460 --> 00:44.753
Fuck this shit.

00:45.628 --> 00:46.463
Let's go.

00:48.089 --> 00:48.923
[Gun-woo] Oh…

00:52.761 --> 00:54.471
Bro, we gotta call an ambulance.

00:54.554 --> 00:57.015
That's a bad idea, Gun-woo.

00:57.098 --> 00:59.684
Dude, this guy is dying. [breathes deeply]

01:02.604 --> 01:04.189
- [engine revs]
- [sirens wailing]

01:15.825 --> 01:16.826
[Gun-woo] Uh, Hyeon-ju,

01:16.910 --> 01:18.995
a homeless old man
was injured really badly,

01:19.079 --> 01:20.413
so we called an ambulance.

01:21.247 --> 01:24.459
- What about Yang Jae-myeong?
- Uh, he ran away.

01:24.542 --> 01:26.503
Goddammit! I told you not to get involved.

01:26.586 --> 01:28.546
I mean, he was really badly hurt.

01:28.630 --> 01:29.506
We had no choice.

01:29.589 --> 01:32.133
You don't even know the guy,
so why would you interfere? Damn it!

01:32.217 --> 01:34.636
- Uh, I know, but we--
- [phone line beeping]

01:39.224 --> 01:40.141
So what should we do?

01:45.438 --> 01:46.397
I'll give her a call.

01:52.195 --> 01:53.988
[sighs] What?

01:54.072 --> 01:58.201
Yes, Hyeon-ju, uh, about this…
We are really, really sorry.

01:58.284 --> 02:00.328
This was totally our fault 100 times over.

02:00.411 --> 02:03.039
Where are you right now?
Just let me apologize to you in person.

02:03.123 --> 02:04.916
Forget it. It's over.

02:05.458 --> 02:08.128
Please, Hyeon-ju,
just give us five minutes.

02:08.628 --> 02:12.006
We just… feel really badly,
and I'm sorry about the whole thing.

02:12.590 --> 02:14.425
Gun-woo also wants to apologize.

02:14.509 --> 02:16.761
- Please, just give us five minutes.
- [sighs]

02:17.345 --> 02:18.179
Come on.

02:18.680 --> 02:19.973
Meet me at the bookstore.

02:21.266 --> 02:22.350
[sighs]

02:23.226 --> 02:25.728
[engine revs]

02:31.109 --> 02:32.110
[Woo-jin sighs]

02:32.193 --> 02:33.236
Dude, look…

02:35.572 --> 02:37.323
To be honest with you,
I really don't get it.

02:37.407 --> 02:38.616
What don't you get, huh?

02:39.242 --> 02:41.119
I mean,
if we didn't do anything to help him,

02:41.202 --> 02:42.829
that old man would've definitely died.

02:42.912 --> 02:43.746
You saw it yourself.

02:44.330 --> 02:45.165
I did.

02:45.248 --> 02:47.167
So if saving that man was the right thing,

02:47.250 --> 02:49.002
why did you have to apologize
for what we did?

02:49.085 --> 02:52.088
- Why do we have to say we're sorry?
- This was our first time on the job.

02:52.589 --> 02:55.341
Hyeon-ju wasn't there, so it's hard
for her to understand what happened.

02:55.425 --> 02:57.302
She's still learning how we respond.

02:57.385 --> 02:59.512
That's why she got mad
when things didn't go as planned,

02:59.596 --> 03:02.724
but if we apologize and take the blame,
I think she'll be cool,

03:02.807 --> 03:04.642
and at the end,
hopefully she'll trust us more.

03:06.603 --> 03:08.605
- But…
- Gun-woo.

03:08.688 --> 03:11.733
I know you didn't do anything wrong.
I was right there with you.

03:11.816 --> 03:13.651
But thinking about it as a job,

03:14.360 --> 03:17.405
a new job with a new boss,
we should try to smooth it over.

03:18.406 --> 03:20.325
Just this once, okay?

03:22.368 --> 03:23.912
Yeah, okay.

03:23.995 --> 03:25.330
[theme music playing]

03:48.937 --> 03:52.315
BLOODHOUNDS

04:00.323 --> 04:02.700
Don't sit. This won't take long.

04:03.409 --> 04:05.370
You fought Yang Jae-myeong, didn't you?

04:05.870 --> 04:07.872
We had no choice, so… so yeah.

04:07.956 --> 04:09.624
We can't work together anymore.

04:10.416 --> 04:11.251
[Gun-woo gasps]

04:12.168 --> 04:14.796
What? Isn't it obvious?

04:15.380 --> 04:16.881
I mean, we said we were sorry.

04:16.965 --> 04:18.800
I don't need an apology!

04:19.300 --> 04:20.301
[sighs]

04:20.385 --> 04:23.179
Yang Jae-myeong saw your faces, didn't he?

04:24.097 --> 04:25.890
- My plan was to quietly tail him…
- [sighs]

04:25.974 --> 04:26.808
…and gather evidence,

04:26.891 --> 04:29.394
but now that he knows someone's on to him,
he'll probably lie low,

04:29.477 --> 04:30.561
and who knows for long.

04:30.645 --> 04:33.398
So, because of you, my plan is ruined.

04:33.481 --> 04:35.858
We wore caps and masks.
He couldn't have seen our faces.

04:35.942 --> 04:39.487
Oh! You covered your face
then there's no way he can recognize you.

04:39.570 --> 04:42.156
Since this shitty hair was covered up,
you have an amazing disguise.

04:42.240 --> 04:44.617
Goddammit! I would recognize you
from a mile away!

04:44.701 --> 04:47.870
[panting] Well? Get out.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.205
- We apologized.
- I said get out!

04:49.289 --> 04:51.708
- We had no choice given the situation.
- What situation?

04:51.791 --> 04:53.251
It's our first time working together.

04:53.334 --> 04:55.211
- You can't expect perfection.
- That's why I refused you!

04:55.295 --> 04:57.797
- We did what we thought was right.
- What situation warrants that?

04:57.880 --> 04:59.215
- I told you earlier.
- Do you not hear me?

04:59.299 --> 05:01.968
- What does my hair have to do with it?
- We'll go. We'll go.

05:02.051 --> 05:03.845
We'll leave right now,
so please stop shouting.

05:05.847 --> 05:07.223
I will find a way to return

05:08.558 --> 05:10.727
the hundred million that Mr. Choi gave me.

05:12.770 --> 05:17.358
But… since Woo-jin and I just listened
to you yelling at us,

05:18.401 --> 05:19.986
please listen to one thing I have to say.

05:20.903 --> 05:21.738
[scoffs]

05:26.367 --> 05:28.828
If someone offered
to make your work go smoothly

05:30.705 --> 05:32.332
in exchange for killing someone,

05:33.416 --> 05:34.500
could you do it?

05:37.545 --> 05:38.504
[exhales sharply]

05:47.680 --> 05:49.682
That boss of Smile Capital
did this to my face.

05:51.809 --> 05:54.395
If I had done nothing
when a man was dying in front of me,

05:55.188 --> 05:57.815
then don't you think
I'd be even worse than that guy.

05:59.317 --> 06:00.735
It would have been wrong.

06:03.446 --> 06:04.822
Please just think about it.

06:18.753 --> 06:19.587
[door opens]

06:20.963 --> 06:21.923
[door closes]

06:40.233 --> 06:41.859
I'll find something else.

06:41.943 --> 06:43.069
Don't worry too much.

06:44.487 --> 06:46.739
I'm sorry. I couldn't hold myself back.

06:47.448 --> 06:49.325
[Woo-jin] You held back better than I did.

06:50.785 --> 06:53.704
You hungry?
I know this 24-hour soup place. Let's go.

06:55.498 --> 06:56.749
[groans] Wait.

06:58.000 --> 07:00.628
It's probably closed because of COVID.
It's past ten.

07:02.088 --> 07:02.922
[Gun-woo sighs]

07:03.005 --> 07:05.216
Well that just made me hungry for nothing.

07:05.800 --> 07:06.676
I forgot.

07:09.720 --> 07:11.305
[groans] My stomach hurts.

07:12.890 --> 07:15.226
Hey, it isn't my fault they're closed
because of COVID.

07:16.269 --> 07:18.062
Well, it is your fault for bringing it up.

07:19.439 --> 07:22.316
Hey, you also couldn't hold yourself back
with her.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.235
You just said
I did a good job holding back.

07:24.318 --> 07:25.570
I only said it because I felt bad.

07:25.653 --> 07:28.448
- You were moping like a goddamn loser.
- I wasn't moping like a goddamn loser.

07:29.115 --> 07:32.785
[mocking] "I wasn't moping
like a goddamn loser."

07:33.786 --> 07:34.912
What are you doing?

07:34.996 --> 07:37.999
[mocking] I'm imitating you, you loser.
"God, I'm hungry."

07:38.082 --> 07:40.501
- "Oh, my stomach hurts." [whimpers]
- Wow.

07:40.585 --> 07:42.086
Dude, that's pretty harsh.

07:44.297 --> 07:45.882
You can't even take a joke now?

07:45.965 --> 07:48.509
Huh? You weren't joking.
That was totally serious.

07:49.594 --> 07:52.555
Hey, I'm seriously offended.
Apologize to me.

07:52.638 --> 07:53.973
- [phone vibrates, chimes]
- [sighs]

07:58.352 --> 08:01.272
SORRY, I WAS WRONG. SEE YOU AT THE OFFICE
TOMORROW AT 10:00 A.M.

08:02.231 --> 08:03.065
[gasps]

08:04.984 --> 08:08.362
- I knew this would happen.
- [shouting]

08:15.411 --> 08:17.580
[breathes deeply]

08:18.831 --> 08:20.249
[gentle piano music playing]

08:50.363 --> 08:51.239
[golf ball hit]

08:51.322 --> 08:54.325
Yeah! It's short. It's short. It's short.

08:54.408 --> 08:55.409
- Super short.
- Super short!

08:55.493 --> 08:57.745
- Fuck! Will you shut the fuck up?
- Get out of here, loser.

08:57.828 --> 09:00.373
- [mocking] "Will you shut the fuck up?"
- Why are you mad? It's just a game.

09:00.456 --> 09:01.958
- Calm down.
- It's your turn. Go!

09:02.041 --> 09:03.751
- [man] Watch it.
- Okay, I will.

09:03.834 --> 09:05.628
- [mocking] Your turn.
- [In-yeong] Fuck off.

09:05.711 --> 09:06.671
YANG JAE-MYEONG
I'M WAITING IN FRONT OF THE GOLF SHOP

09:06.754 --> 09:07.588
[man] Stop swearing.

09:07.672 --> 09:09.966
- [woman] You have to wear your mask, sir.
- Sure thing.

09:14.053 --> 09:15.096
What is it?

09:15.930 --> 09:18.057
[Jae-myeong]
Sir, someone was following us.

09:19.725 --> 09:20.601
Who was it?

09:21.310 --> 09:23.980
They were young,
but they seemed to know how to fight.

09:24.897 --> 09:25.731
Are you sure?

09:25.815 --> 09:26.649
Huh?

09:26.732 --> 09:28.609
You sure someone was following you,
you idiot?!

09:28.693 --> 09:30.111
[Jae-myeong breathes shallowly]

09:30.611 --> 09:31.487
Focus.

09:31.571 --> 09:32.572
Uh, the thing is…

09:33.781 --> 09:34.615
Talk.

09:35.283 --> 09:37.285
Before I started working for you, sir,

09:37.368 --> 09:38.869
I sort of borrowed money from a place.

09:38.953 --> 09:41.080
The fuckers didn't say anything,
so I just ignored them.

09:41.163 --> 09:42.248
Talk faster.

09:42.331 --> 09:44.458
But those guys
came for the money recently.

09:44.542 --> 09:47.545
The bastard that came over
was wearing a hat with a red cat on it.

09:47.628 --> 09:50.840
And one of the punks who jumped us
was wearing the same hat.

09:53.926 --> 09:55.011
You sure it's him?

09:56.762 --> 09:58.264
It was the same hat, sir.

10:02.810 --> 10:04.228
Where did you borrow the money from?

10:04.312 --> 10:06.814
[Woo-jin] So basically,
this is what happened yesterday.

10:07.481 --> 10:10.443
Yang Jae-myeong had already robbed
that homeless man of his ID,

10:10.526 --> 10:11.611
but he had forgotten,

10:11.694 --> 10:14.363
and he tried to con him again,
which ended up in a fight.

10:16.073 --> 10:18.034
Uh, but just how much money

10:18.117 --> 10:20.870
do Jae-myeong's guys borrow
with one stolen ID?

10:21.787 --> 10:23.706
About 50 million won per fake account.

10:24.373 --> 10:26.167
That's 500 million for ten IDs.

10:26.250 --> 10:28.419
Jesus. How long have they been doing this?

10:29.754 --> 10:31.756
I think at least for half a year, yeah.

10:31.839 --> 10:34.592
Wow! They must have made a small fortune.

10:35.092 --> 10:36.010
Hm.

10:36.093 --> 10:39.180
But those loan sharks that they conned,
did they just sit back and do nothing?

10:39.263 --> 10:41.057
If they call the cops,
they'll be investigated,

10:41.140 --> 10:42.308
so that's not an option.

10:42.391 --> 10:45.019
My take is they're trying to recover
the money on their own but can't.

10:47.480 --> 10:48.522
This is my plan.

10:48.606 --> 10:51.192
Find the private loan sharks
that Yang Jae-myeong conned,

10:51.275 --> 10:54.070
and then we recover the money he stole
for a commission.

10:55.404 --> 10:58.157
With a 1% commission,
we would get three billion won.

10:58.824 --> 10:59.950
We should at least charge 2%.

11:00.034 --> 11:01.661
[uptempo instrumental music playing]

11:06.374 --> 11:07.208
[Gun-woo] Hyung?

11:08.668 --> 11:10.544
If loan sharks get conned,

11:10.628 --> 11:13.631
wouldn't that make things worse
for the people who got loans from them?

11:14.215 --> 11:15.341
Huh?

11:15.424 --> 11:18.427
They might end up torturing their clients
in order to get their money back.

11:19.178 --> 11:20.221
So what?

11:20.304 --> 11:24.392
It's just… I think small business owners
are the ones that will suffer the most.

11:25.559 --> 11:26.977
You're right about that.

11:27.061 --> 11:27.895
Mm.

11:31.357 --> 11:33.442
[tense music playing]

11:40.741 --> 11:42.076
How did they find us?

11:42.910 --> 11:43.786
How did they find us?!

11:44.370 --> 11:45.287
I… I don't know.

11:48.541 --> 11:50.668
Turn off the lights and the sign outside.

11:51.335 --> 11:52.461
[Woo-jin] Damn it!

11:55.506 --> 11:57.758
PYEONGHWA BOOKS

11:59.093 --> 12:00.803
- Turn your phones off for now.
- Okay.

12:08.185 --> 12:10.438
- [Jun-min] It's here? Are you sure?
- Yes. I'm sure, sir.

12:19.155 --> 12:21.240
You borrowed money from a bookstore?

12:21.323 --> 12:24.994
Yeah, the owner here used to be
a big moneylender back in the day.

12:29.999 --> 12:31.000
[music intensifies]

12:37.423 --> 12:38.716
[inhales deeply]

12:41.886 --> 12:43.929
Hey, give this a kick here.

12:51.270 --> 12:52.354
[Hyeon-ju exhales sharply]

12:54.064 --> 12:54.940
Try this.

12:57.276 --> 12:58.944
Come on. Hurry up, you idiot.

13:00.279 --> 13:01.238
Ow. [groaning]

13:06.118 --> 13:07.870
- Kick harder.
- Huh?

13:07.953 --> 13:09.580
Kick harder, you asshole!

13:09.663 --> 13:12.374
Uh… [grunting]

13:12.458 --> 13:13.334
[Jun-min] Harder!

13:14.376 --> 13:15.628
- Harder!
- [kicking continues]

13:15.711 --> 13:17.296
Kick fucking harder!

13:18.172 --> 13:19.340
[Jae-myeong grunting]

13:21.759 --> 13:23.844
- Stop. That's enough.
- [panting]

13:23.928 --> 13:26.305
We'll need something stronger
to tear this down.

13:29.016 --> 13:30.351
This here is the safe.

13:30.434 --> 13:31.894
[panting]

13:37.191 --> 13:38.776
[suspenseful music playing]

14:01.924 --> 14:03.425
[suspenseful music ends]

14:03.509 --> 14:04.802
[Woo-jin inhales sharply]

14:05.553 --> 14:06.679
[Woo-jin exhales]

14:07.304 --> 14:08.639
[Woo-jin and Gun-woo sigh]

14:10.140 --> 14:13.894
Last night on your way back,
did you check if you were being followed?

14:15.062 --> 14:17.314
Uh, well, we took the bus.

14:17.898 --> 14:20.109
You realize
they could have followed the bus.

14:20.192 --> 14:24.947
If they had followed us last night,
why didn't they jump us right away?

14:25.030 --> 14:26.615
Why decide to make their move now?

14:27.199 --> 14:30.077
- He might've wanted to bring Kim Jun-min--
- Whoa, no, Hyeon-ju.

14:30.160 --> 14:32.371
Yang Jae-myeong saw
how we fought last night.

14:32.454 --> 14:35.124
If he was planning on jumping us,
he would've brought more muscle.

14:35.708 --> 14:38.419
[inhales sharply] I bet…
they weren't sure.

14:38.919 --> 14:42.506
But now,
they might have caught onto something.

14:43.340 --> 14:44.216
[sighs]

14:46.760 --> 14:50.472
In any case, we need to figure out
how they found out about this place.

14:50.556 --> 14:53.017
That's how
we don't make the same mistake twice

14:53.100 --> 14:54.643
Okay. That's a good idea.

14:54.727 --> 14:58.230
Why don't we sit down
and talk it through, hm?

14:59.023 --> 14:59.857
Hm.

15:02.693 --> 15:04.695
[suspenseful music playing]

15:05.738 --> 15:08.365
Does Yang Jae-myeong
know about this place?

15:09.033 --> 15:10.492
He came here a long time ago.

15:11.911 --> 15:16.081
That means he's caught onto
our connection here somehow.

15:16.582 --> 15:17.958
- Oh!
- Huh?

15:20.419 --> 15:21.545
Oh!

15:25.883 --> 15:26.717
Uh…

15:27.927 --> 15:30.137
Hyeon-ju, I think
he may have recognized your cap.

15:31.597 --> 15:33.766
The thing is,

15:33.849 --> 15:35.392
I followed you a while back

15:35.476 --> 15:37.603
when I saw you chasing down
a homeless man.

15:37.686 --> 15:38.771
Wait…

15:40.272 --> 15:42.942
Yeah, that was me. [imitates taser]

15:43.525 --> 15:45.778
The homeless man back then
was Yang Jae-myeong.

15:46.362 --> 15:47.863
Oh, wow.

15:47.947 --> 15:51.408
Uh… I was wearing
that cap back then, wasn't I?

15:51.992 --> 15:54.745
Uh, yes,
I definitely remember seeing it on you.

15:54.828 --> 15:55.788
[sighs]

15:56.288 --> 15:58.499
Then that might've been
how they found out.

15:58.582 --> 16:01.961
Okay, but why do you think
they kicked the shutters.

16:02.544 --> 16:05.839
Our shutters were custom-made
with steel, not aluminum.

16:05.923 --> 16:07.341
I think they were checking for that.

16:07.424 --> 16:09.843
[exhales sharply] I think they'll be back.

16:12.221 --> 16:13.263
Why is he here?

16:13.931 --> 16:15.307
[Woo-jin breathing rapidly]

16:16.517 --> 16:17.559
[sighs] Damn it.

16:30.990 --> 16:33.033
What have you done? [panting]

16:33.117 --> 16:34.952
That white car came here, didn't it?

16:36.537 --> 16:37.788
Are you not going to talk?

16:41.166 --> 16:43.752
I am sorry, sir. It's entirely my fault.

16:44.670 --> 16:47.798
The two of us…
We went on a job last night.

16:47.881 --> 16:49.049
What job?

16:49.133 --> 16:51.593
Uh, the thing is…

16:53.595 --> 16:54.471
What job was that?

16:56.515 --> 16:58.100
We were tailing Yang Jae-myeong.

16:59.226 --> 17:00.477
- Why?
- [Hyeon-ju] Grandpa.

17:00.561 --> 17:02.855
Loan sharks are desperate
to catch Yang Jae-myeong.

17:02.938 --> 17:05.065
I'm sure they'll be willing to pay for it.

17:05.899 --> 17:08.235
And I believe I'm the only one
who is able to catch him.

17:09.153 --> 17:10.487
Are you doing this to make money?

17:10.571 --> 17:12.322
It's good to make money.

17:14.074 --> 17:15.451
And what did you guys do?

17:16.452 --> 17:19.121
It's my… friends' job
to protect me, right?

17:19.705 --> 17:21.498
[sighs] Well, they did.

17:22.833 --> 17:24.293
I'm disappointed in you.

17:26.253 --> 17:28.255
Yeah, well,
I'm disappointed in you too, Grandpa.

17:28.338 --> 17:30.466
It's clear Yang Jae-myeong
is up to no good,

17:30.549 --> 17:31.925
so why aren't you doing anything?

17:32.009 --> 17:35.471
With your orders, Mr. Hwang could
get rid of a loser like him immediately.

17:35.554 --> 17:38.432
So you're frustrated?
Well, I'm even more frustrated!

17:39.850 --> 17:42.603
Go ahead.
Take off that bandage on your face.

17:42.686 --> 17:44.438
- Hm?
- Hurry up and do it.

17:46.023 --> 17:47.024
[Gun-woo exhales]

17:50.736 --> 17:53.864
If Yang Jae-myeong and Kim Jun-min
keep scamming private loan sharks,

17:54.698 --> 17:58.702
they'll keep threatening and harassing
powerless people like Gun-woo here.

17:59.328 --> 18:03.123
That's going to make
all the charity work you do meaningless.

18:03.207 --> 18:06.085
Your money will go straight
into their pockets!

18:06.752 --> 18:09.338
If you really want
to help out those in need,

18:09.421 --> 18:12.549
you should weed out the punks
like Yang Jae-myeong first.

18:14.426 --> 18:16.095
Who did that to Gun-woo's face?

18:18.847 --> 18:20.557
The boss of Smile Capital did it, sir.

18:22.101 --> 18:22.935
And his name?

18:23.894 --> 18:26.105
Uh, well, I don't know his name, sir.

18:26.897 --> 18:29.733
But he had a long knife scar
running down his left cheek.

18:30.734 --> 18:32.069
[ominous music playing]

18:38.909 --> 18:39.993
You guys head back now.

18:52.881 --> 18:54.424
[groans]

18:57.719 --> 19:01.598
Sir, could it just be a coincidence?

19:02.099 --> 19:05.477
Please check whether Kim Myeong-gil
is the CEO of Smile Capital.

19:05.978 --> 19:06.812
[man] Yes, sir.

19:14.194 --> 19:16.238
Juju.

19:17.489 --> 19:20.617
- Getting too comfortable, aren't we?
- I mean, you called us friends before.

19:20.701 --> 19:22.870
I have to say, that felt good.

19:23.370 --> 19:24.371
So?

19:24.454 --> 19:27.916
So I thought it might be nice
to talk more casually with each other.

19:28.000 --> 19:30.002
We are a team, after all, Juju.

19:30.085 --> 19:32.629
Hm, we're not a team
if we don't speak casually?

19:32.713 --> 19:34.089
I'm just saying it would be nice

19:34.173 --> 19:35.799
if we acted more
like one big happy family.

19:35.883 --> 19:37.134
It's just a suggestion.

19:37.217 --> 19:40.888
Well, if we're family,
the oldest would treat the rest to a meal.

19:40.971 --> 19:42.097
So will you be buying?

19:42.723 --> 19:45.017
Uh, I actually prefer formalities, ma'am.

19:45.100 --> 19:46.768
[laughs] I'm kidding. Relax.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.104
Let's use Grandpa's credit card.
What do you guys want?

19:49.188 --> 19:50.022
Rib eye.

19:50.731 --> 19:51.565
Then you pay.

19:53.025 --> 19:54.276
Uh, barbecue buffet.

19:54.359 --> 19:57.446
- A barbecue buffet?
- Yeah, I know a really great place.

19:59.698 --> 20:00.991
[imitates scissors cutting]

20:01.074 --> 20:02.576
Mm, sure.

20:02.659 --> 20:03.493
Let's go!

20:06.747 --> 20:08.999
How long have you been friends
with Gun-woo?

20:09.958 --> 20:13.253
I don't think it really matters
how long you've known a person.

20:13.337 --> 20:16.089
Just knowing someone for a while
doesn't mean they're your friend.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.007
Okay.

20:17.090 --> 20:21.762
What really matters is how similar
your life trajectories have been.

20:21.845 --> 20:23.764
So even if it's a short conversation,

20:23.847 --> 20:25.849
you gain a deep understanding
of each other.

20:25.933 --> 20:27.392
That's what matters.

20:27.476 --> 20:29.645
- That's the relationship you guys have?
- Right.

20:29.728 --> 20:31.521
It's like we're boxers,

20:31.605 --> 20:34.399
but we exchange a lot more
than just our fists. Pow!

20:34.983 --> 20:36.985
"So that's the kind of life you've lived."

20:37.069 --> 20:37.903
Pow!

20:37.986 --> 20:39.529
"Well, this is how I lived, you punk."

20:39.613 --> 20:45.285
Each blow contains
both fighters' character, heart,

20:45.369 --> 20:48.497
history, history,

20:49.248 --> 20:50.123
History?

20:50.749 --> 20:51.917
History.

20:53.210 --> 20:54.711
We see it all.

20:54.795 --> 20:55.879
We know. Mm.

20:56.755 --> 20:57.589
Sure.

20:57.673 --> 20:59.549
And besides, Gun-woo is…

21:01.551 --> 21:02.886
a senior Marine.

21:04.221 --> 21:06.014
And that tells you everything.

21:06.682 --> 21:08.225
What exactly does it tell you?

21:10.018 --> 21:11.144
Everything.

21:11.228 --> 21:12.437
Everything about what?

21:12.521 --> 21:15.607
Juju, this isn't something
I just can't easily explain to you.

21:15.691 --> 21:17.317
It's just, you know, a Marine thing.

21:17.401 --> 21:21.238
It's like when rappers use hip-hop
as an all-encompassing term

21:21.321 --> 21:23.657
when they look at something
and go, "This is hip-hop."

21:23.740 --> 21:25.284
It's indescribable.

21:25.367 --> 21:27.911
Oh, indescribable, you say?

21:28.704 --> 21:30.998
- Are you being sarcastic?
- Who? Me?

21:31.081 --> 21:32.416
Hey, this stuff is really…

21:32.499 --> 21:33.625
- Here we go.
- Right.

21:37.838 --> 21:38.672
Huh?

21:39.464 --> 21:41.925
[sighs] Dude,
you haven't turned on the grill yet?

21:42.009 --> 21:43.176
You didn't tell me to.

21:43.260 --> 21:45.971
Come on, man. Whoever is sitting down
is supposed to get the grill going.

21:46.054 --> 21:48.348
I didn't know that.
Why didn't you turn it when we got here?

21:48.432 --> 21:51.518
Because the grill would've burned up
in the time it took to return with meat.

21:51.601 --> 21:53.312
How would a grill burn up?

21:53.395 --> 21:56.648
[sighs] Well, technically,
the grill itself doesn't burn.

21:56.732 --> 21:58.942
The meat would burn
the second you place it on the grill.

21:59.026 --> 22:00.152
You're talking about meat burning?

22:00.235 --> 22:02.446
That's what people mean
when they say they're burning the grill.

22:02.529 --> 22:05.741
Well, that's insider lingo for people
who work at barbecue restaurants.

22:05.824 --> 22:07.743
My mom also refers to it
as "burning the grill."

22:07.826 --> 22:09.703
- Well, my mom doesn't.
- [sighs]

22:10.287 --> 22:12.080
- [Woo-jin] For someone who knows meat--
- There!

22:12.706 --> 22:13.707
Get grilling.

22:13.790 --> 22:15.167
Uh, no.

22:15.250 --> 22:18.128
It's too soon for the meat.
Can't put it on a lukewarm grill.

22:18.211 --> 22:19.838
That would ruin the flavor.
You gotta wait.

22:20.714 --> 22:22.174
[breathes deeply]

22:22.799 --> 22:25.177
Shall we maybe converse
while the grill is heating up?

22:26.094 --> 22:29.514
Gun-woo, just speak naturally for once.

22:29.598 --> 22:31.391
Uh, so are you and Mr. Choi related?

22:31.975 --> 22:34.603
Huh? Well, that came out of left field.

22:34.686 --> 22:36.146
I've wanted to know too.

22:36.229 --> 22:37.898
Since the very beginning, Juju.

22:39.816 --> 22:40.650
Well…

22:41.902 --> 22:43.487
[sighs] …long story short…

22:46.114 --> 22:48.533
I was diagnosed with spinal cancer
when I was eight.

22:49.701 --> 22:51.495
I was cured by the time I was ten,

22:53.747 --> 22:55.999
but then… my dad died.

22:57.167 --> 22:59.795
- [exhales]
- So I was sent to an orphanage,

23:01.171 --> 23:03.131
I hated it so much that I ran away.

23:04.299 --> 23:06.093
I used to get so hungry, you know,

23:07.135 --> 23:10.722
that I ate leftover jjajangmyeon
that people left on their doorstep.

23:11.473 --> 23:13.725
I also worked at bars
with other runaway kids,

23:14.976 --> 23:16.603
but I couldn't do it anymore.

23:16.686 --> 23:18.355
[gentle piano music playing]

23:18.438 --> 23:20.023
So I returned to the orphanage.

23:22.275 --> 23:25.529
But I was then dragged off
to a different orphanage when I was 17.

23:26.446 --> 23:28.365
And Grandpa happened to be
the owner there.

23:28.448 --> 23:30.325
- You mean Mr. Choi?
- Yes.

23:31.326 --> 23:34.204
He said he built an orphanage
because he wanted to do something good.

23:36.123 --> 23:38.166
He was really nice to me in particular.

23:38.792 --> 23:40.752
So at first,
I thought he might be a pervert, but…

23:42.754 --> 23:44.256
I came to know as time passed…

23:46.425 --> 23:48.093
that he was being sincere.

23:48.176 --> 23:50.720
Grandpa paid for me
to learn everything I know now.

23:50.804 --> 23:52.264
because I didn't have the money.

23:52.347 --> 23:56.101
I learned kendo, how to ride a motorcycle.

24:01.982 --> 24:04.776
I could tell immediately
that Mr. Choi is really a nice person.

24:05.485 --> 24:06.778
Since middle school,

24:06.862 --> 24:09.906
I've been working part-time jobs
to pay off my dad's debt.

24:09.990 --> 24:12.659
[exhales sharply]
But when our debt got to 100 million won,

24:12.742 --> 24:14.411
I suddenly felt totally helpless.

24:15.370 --> 24:18.206
So I know how scary
a hundred million won can be.

24:18.707 --> 24:21.877
And when Mr. Choi gave me that money,
telling me to pay off my debts,

24:21.960 --> 24:23.211
I thought to myself,

24:24.296 --> 24:26.923
I have to make sure to protect this man
at all costs.

24:29.134 --> 24:32.762
Grandpa told me that
in order to judge someone's character,

24:32.846 --> 24:34.431
one should open up your heart.

24:34.514 --> 24:37.058
That people with character
will see your sincerity

24:37.142 --> 24:38.143
and return it in kind,

24:38.935 --> 24:41.354
and those who lack depth
will try to use that against you.

24:42.606 --> 24:44.608
- Agreed.
- You're a nice person, Gun-woo.

24:45.233 --> 24:49.154
Thanks. Two things I'm good at
are being nice and being diligent.

24:49.779 --> 24:51.656
- I think we can start grilling now.
- Mm-hm.

24:51.740 --> 24:53.408
[soft instrumental music playing]

24:53.492 --> 24:55.619
[meat sizzling]

24:58.872 --> 25:00.499
[Woo-jin] Ah!

25:00.582 --> 25:04.127
- Ah, perfect timing. Very nice.
- You're getting pretty good at this.

25:04.211 --> 25:06.338
Well, I mean,
I learned from the best, right? [laughs]

25:06.963 --> 25:09.424
Wow, I'm feeling so left out
all of a sudden.

25:10.300 --> 25:11.801
Sheesh, never mind. [groans]

25:11.885 --> 25:12.719
Hurry up and flip it.

25:12.802 --> 25:15.180
- I can't do that yet.
- You gotta trust him. He's good at this.

25:15.263 --> 25:17.933
[scoffs] Sorry,
I didn't know he was the grill master.

25:18.016 --> 25:19.142
You will soon.

25:19.226 --> 25:21.186
- [grunts]
- [chuckles]

25:21.269 --> 25:23.063
[Woo-jin inhales sharply] Smells amazing!

25:23.563 --> 25:24.814
Oh! [inhales sharply]

25:25.315 --> 25:26.358
Let's clean out the buffet.

25:26.441 --> 25:27.442
- [Gun-woo] Sure.
- [laughs]

25:28.026 --> 25:30.195
- When are those stitches coming off?
- Tomorrow morning.

25:30.278 --> 25:31.279
Does it hurt?

25:31.363 --> 25:32.864
Not too bad.

25:32.948 --> 25:33.823
[Woo-jin exhales]

25:33.907 --> 25:37.118
- [groans] I asked for mine hot.
- You're supposed to take your coffee cold.

25:37.202 --> 25:38.912
Seriously? Come on.

25:39.538 --> 25:40.705
- Hyeon-ju.
- Yeah?

25:40.789 --> 25:42.624
Yang Jae-myeong knows
where the bookstore is.

25:42.707 --> 25:44.251
Shouldn't we do something about it?

25:45.627 --> 25:47.629
[sighs] I'll talk it over with Grandpa.

25:48.171 --> 25:50.840
[Woo-jin sighs] You should ask him soon.
We don't have time.

25:50.924 --> 25:51.758
[Hyeon-ju] Okay.

25:53.635 --> 25:54.594
[Mr. Hong] Ms. Lee.

25:55.095 --> 25:57.347
The lobby is a hotel's first impression.

25:57.430 --> 25:59.182
I want us to impress
our international guests

25:59.266 --> 26:01.434
with the most beautiful,
stunning Korean experience

26:01.518 --> 26:02.519
they've ever encountered.

26:02.602 --> 26:04.354
Something
they've never experienced before.

26:04.437 --> 26:05.397
That kind of thing.

26:05.480 --> 26:06.690
[Ms. Lee] Yes, I understand.

26:06.773 --> 26:07.816
TEAM LEADER LEE SO-HYEON

26:07.899 --> 26:10.610
Anyway, I look forward to hearing
your brilliant ideas.

26:10.694 --> 26:12.070
See you tomorrow morning.

26:12.153 --> 26:14.614
Our casino will be
on the top floor of that hotel.

26:14.698 --> 26:19.119
My goal is a hundred billion
in annual revenue.

26:19.202 --> 26:20.829
There are a lot of people
itching for a fix

26:20.912 --> 26:24.207
now that gambling in Macau
has been blocked off due to COVID.

26:24.791 --> 26:29.254
We'll secretly book them a suite
every week and let them have fun

26:30.255 --> 26:32.674
while secretly catching their gambling
on camera.

26:32.757 --> 26:35.468
Afterward, once we have enough cash,

26:36.136 --> 26:39.639
Jang-do will make sure
to hand over to the police

26:40.307 --> 26:41.850
all evidence of gambling.

26:41.933 --> 26:43.101
[ominous music playing]

26:43.602 --> 26:46.104
When the hotel is ruined
and worth nothing,

26:47.063 --> 26:50.900
we'll swoop in
and take over the whole thing. [laughs]

26:57.699 --> 27:00.035
We need to be ready
to spend a hundred billion

27:00.118 --> 27:02.829
by the time Jang-do returns
with dirt on Director Hong.

27:03.330 --> 27:06.082
We're 50 billion short, right?

27:06.166 --> 27:07.000
Yes.

27:08.710 --> 27:10.670
Now it's time to collect on everything.

27:11.880 --> 27:14.382
Sell off anything that's of any value.

27:16.092 --> 27:17.510
[employee] Coming through!

27:24.309 --> 27:25.268
Yes, sir.

27:25.352 --> 27:27.854
Yes, that car you mentioned before
just came in.

27:27.937 --> 27:29.105
Cool.

27:30.440 --> 27:31.858
I'll be right back, sir.

27:32.651 --> 27:34.069
[tense music playing]

27:35.612 --> 27:36.446
[chuckles]

27:43.745 --> 27:44.996
What the…

27:51.336 --> 27:52.170
CAR WASH EXIT
NO PARKING

27:53.380 --> 27:54.214
Hello!

27:56.216 --> 27:58.093
[groans] Damn it.

28:00.845 --> 28:01.721
[laughs]

28:02.430 --> 28:04.099
[Mr. Hong groans, grunts]

28:05.433 --> 28:07.143
[Mr. Hong groans]

28:07.644 --> 28:08.853
[goons grunting]

28:08.937 --> 28:11.189
[grunting]

28:12.691 --> 28:15.276
- [screaming]
- [goon 1] All right, keep him down.

28:15.860 --> 28:17.112
- [goon 2 grunts]
- [groans]

28:17.612 --> 28:18.738
- [goons laughing]
- [coughs]

28:18.822 --> 28:20.031
[goon 3] Look at him! [laughs]

28:22.492 --> 28:23.660
[retching]

28:26.287 --> 28:27.497
You want more, huh?

28:28.081 --> 28:30.250
- [grunting]
- [goon 1] Grab him.

28:31.084 --> 28:32.711
[groans, whimpers]

28:33.294 --> 28:35.463
- [grunting]
- [goons laughing]

28:35.547 --> 28:37.257
Hey, strip him down.

28:38.007 --> 28:41.094
[screaming]

28:46.433 --> 28:47.267
[employee] Ah.

28:48.017 --> 28:49.769
- He's this way.
- [Jang-do] Is he in there now?

28:49.853 --> 28:51.730
- [employee] Yes.
- Thank you for your hard work.

28:51.813 --> 28:52.856
[employee chuckles softly]

28:54.107 --> 28:56.109
- You can count it.
- Thank you, sir.

28:56.192 --> 28:58.361
- [goons laughing]
- [goon 1] Look at him.

28:58.445 --> 29:00.739
[Mr. Hong whimpering]

29:02.657 --> 29:03.700
[goon 1] Hey. Hey, shh.

29:03.783 --> 29:05.702
[Jang-do] Whoa!
You boys sure did a number on him.

29:05.785 --> 29:06.995
- Hello, sir!
- Hello, sir!

29:07.078 --> 29:08.121
I'm so cold.

29:08.204 --> 29:10.498
Can I please have
something to wear? Please.

29:10.582 --> 29:11.624
God, I'm… I'm sorry, sir.

29:12.292 --> 29:13.585
[ominous music playing]

29:13.668 --> 29:14.961
[sobbing]

29:16.504 --> 29:17.422
Hi there.

29:21.176 --> 29:23.636
- You… [panting]
- [chuckles]

29:23.720 --> 29:25.847
You, it's you, isn't it? Fuck.

29:25.930 --> 29:27.098
- [winces]
- Motherfucker!

29:27.182 --> 29:28.391
[Mr. Hong sobbing]

29:28.475 --> 29:31.227
Jesus, not too long ago,
you were acting like hot shit.

29:32.604 --> 29:33.438
Prick.

29:34.105 --> 29:34.939
So,

29:35.982 --> 29:38.610
you really shouldn't have fucked around
with him.

29:39.235 --> 29:41.404
- [groans]
- Did you think he would get scared

29:41.488 --> 29:46.201
and apologize to you or something
just because your cousin's a cop? Huh?

29:46.284 --> 29:49.370
- [Mr. Hong sobbing]
- [scoffs]

29:49.871 --> 29:50.705
[groans]

29:52.248 --> 29:53.458
[winces]

29:54.918 --> 29:58.755
- Listen, let me teach you a little lesson.
- [groaning]

29:58.838 --> 30:02.842
Wild animals bite back if you hit them.

30:04.552 --> 30:07.972
It doesn't matter how much stronger
or weaker you are than them.

30:08.765 --> 30:10.308
They just bite back.

30:11.392 --> 30:12.852
[panting]

30:14.646 --> 30:16.648
[Mr. Hong groaning]

30:17.315 --> 30:18.900
[Mr. Hong whimpering]

30:18.983 --> 30:20.276
Now then.

30:23.363 --> 30:24.197
Strip down.

30:24.280 --> 30:25.448
What?

30:25.532 --> 30:27.742
Come on, take everything off,
including your underwear.

30:27.826 --> 30:31.496
[spluttering] No, I get it now.
Please, just this once.

30:31.579 --> 30:33.081
- Ugh.
- [Mr. Hong] I'm sorry.

30:33.164 --> 30:35.500
I really don't know what this is about,
but I'm really sorry.

30:35.583 --> 30:36.459
Hey, In-beom.

30:36.543 --> 30:38.670
[shallow breathing]
Please, just this once.

30:39.170 --> 30:40.296
[panting]

30:41.798 --> 30:43.216
[choking]

30:43.299 --> 30:44.509
Wrap it up.

30:46.094 --> 30:47.095
[grunts, groans]

30:53.935 --> 30:54.936
[gasps, groans]

30:55.520 --> 30:56.688
Are you stripping or not?

30:57.313 --> 30:58.147
[grunts]

30:58.731 --> 31:00.108
Don't kill me.

31:00.900 --> 31:03.444
- I guess you're still thirsty.
- [Mr. Hong grunts]

31:06.781 --> 31:09.033
- Oh! [whimpers]
- [Jang-do] What's it gonna be?

31:15.164 --> 31:15.999
[yelps]

31:17.917 --> 31:20.128
- Well…
- I'll strip down! I'll strip down!

31:20.211 --> 31:21.921
[Mr. Hong panting]

31:22.755 --> 31:25.133
[coughing]

31:26.843 --> 31:28.303
[Jang-do] Good call.

31:28.386 --> 31:30.346
Now then, Director Hong,
without further ado,

31:30.430 --> 31:31.556
let's see you strip.

31:31.639 --> 31:33.266
- [goons laughing]
- [groans]

31:33.349 --> 31:34.726
[tense music playing]

31:36.686 --> 31:38.646
[fighters shouting, grunting]

31:40.857 --> 31:43.276
[grunting]

31:49.157 --> 31:50.491
I GOT SOMETHING BIG

31:50.575 --> 31:52.660
All right, that's enough.

32:05.089 --> 32:07.508
- [goons laughing]
- [Mr. Hong groaning]

32:08.134 --> 32:09.510
[Mr. Hong sobbing on video]

32:10.011 --> 32:13.932
[laughing]

32:15.558 --> 32:16.935
[cell phone vibrating]

32:17.018 --> 32:18.061
[exhales deeply]

32:20.772 --> 32:21.606
[exhales]

32:22.607 --> 32:24.359
[vibrating continues]

32:25.485 --> 32:26.319
[grunts]

32:28.947 --> 32:29.864
Yes.

32:29.948 --> 32:31.699
[man] Uh, Mr. Choi,

32:31.783 --> 32:35.995
the Kim Myeong-gil we know
is indeed the CEO of Smile Capital.

32:36.663 --> 32:38.039
Yes, I understand.

32:38.915 --> 32:41.542
I'm coming to pick you up.
I'll be there soon, sir.

32:42.043 --> 32:43.795
Yes. [exhales sharply]

32:46.089 --> 32:46.923
[sighs]

32:49.842 --> 32:51.052
[exhales deeply]

32:57.558 --> 32:58.726
[somber music playing]

33:03.481 --> 33:04.607
[inhales sharply]

33:04.691 --> 33:06.484
I apologize for my sudden decision.

33:09.529 --> 33:12.281
Recently, I've gone through
something very difficult for me.

33:14.283 --> 33:16.703
And I came to this conclusion
after thinking things over,

33:16.786 --> 33:18.204
so I hope you'll understand.

33:19.163 --> 33:21.791
Our company will be terminated
by the end of the month.

33:23.543 --> 33:25.044
I will be wiring you

33:25.795 --> 33:28.339
all of your salary
as well as your severance pay.

33:32.427 --> 33:33.553
Thanks for everything.

33:34.512 --> 33:39.600
Sir, what about… all of our money
that's out there right now?

33:40.476 --> 33:41.811
I'm gonna take care of it.

33:45.982 --> 33:46.899
[door closes]

33:49.318 --> 33:50.236
[sighs]

34:06.502 --> 34:08.588
[child crying]

34:08.671 --> 34:10.465
Papa!

34:11.966 --> 34:13.968
[child crying]

34:15.595 --> 34:18.222
[cell phone vibrating]

34:22.351 --> 34:23.436
[grunts]

34:31.277 --> 34:33.821
- Yes.
- This is Oh In-muk in security, sir.

34:34.405 --> 34:36.449
Some robbers have broken into your office.

34:37.325 --> 34:38.326
How many?

34:39.535 --> 34:40.912
[suspenseful music playing]

34:43.706 --> 34:45.166
[Mr. Oh] I think there are two.

35:00.014 --> 35:02.016
[breathing deeply]

35:04.769 --> 35:05.895
[music intensifies]

35:06.479 --> 35:07.814
[shallow breathing]

35:10.775 --> 35:11.692
[In-beom] Hey!

35:13.277 --> 35:14.362
What's taking you so long?

35:15.321 --> 35:18.449
This model normally comes
with a six-digit combination.

35:18.533 --> 35:19.492
This one has eight.

35:19.575 --> 35:20.952
I think they modified it.

35:22.328 --> 35:24.580
- What does that mean?
- Gonna need more time.

35:25.331 --> 35:26.332
Hurry it up.

35:28.584 --> 35:30.336
[tense music playing]

35:43.891 --> 35:44.767
[chuckles softly]

35:47.395 --> 35:49.397
[exhales, laughs softly]

35:51.065 --> 35:51.899
[man] Got it!

35:53.484 --> 35:54.735
[In-beom] Out of the way.

35:56.279 --> 35:57.530
[breathing rapidly]

36:03.494 --> 36:04.745
PRIVATE LOAN STANDARD AGREEMENT

36:04.829 --> 36:08.040
[man] These promissory notes
are worth a billion won a pop.

36:08.124 --> 36:09.083
Fuck!

36:28.102 --> 36:30.605
No one has come out.
I also held the elevator here.

36:30.688 --> 36:31.856
Thank you.

36:32.440 --> 36:35.234
Uh, shall I accompany you?

36:35.318 --> 36:38.154
Oh, no. I'll be fine. Thank you very much.

36:38.946 --> 36:41.073
Uh, let me just borrow this.

36:41.157 --> 36:41.991
[Mr. Oh] Sure.

36:46.329 --> 36:47.580
[tense music continues]

36:49.749 --> 36:51.709
[In-beom panting]

36:51.792 --> 36:52.835
[door unlocks]

37:03.596 --> 37:04.931
- [music ends]
- [door locks]

37:07.642 --> 37:09.060
[suspenseful music playing]

37:17.860 --> 37:18.945
Who are you?

37:22.990 --> 37:24.116
How did you get in?

37:24.700 --> 37:26.077
[shouts]

37:26.160 --> 37:27.870
[uptempo instrumental music playing]

37:28.829 --> 37:30.039
[both grunting]

37:38.256 --> 37:39.465
- [Mr. Choi grunts]
- [groans]

37:42.802 --> 37:44.720
[grunting]

37:44.804 --> 37:48.307
- [In-beom shouting]
- [grunting]

37:54.105 --> 37:55.815
[Mr. Choi grunting]

37:57.066 --> 37:58.359
[In-beom whimpers]

38:00.069 --> 38:00.903
[man groans]

38:04.740 --> 38:05.950
[man whimpering]

38:06.784 --> 38:08.703
- [Mr. Choi grunts]
- [man groaning]

38:13.833 --> 38:15.209
[man panting]

38:16.210 --> 38:18.087
- [Mr. Choi grunts]
- [man groaning]

38:19.630 --> 38:20.673
Who sent you?

38:21.173 --> 38:22.633
[panting]

38:25.219 --> 38:29.181
- [wincing]
- Who sent you?

38:29.265 --> 38:32.393
- [mumbles, winces]
- Who sent you?

38:32.476 --> 38:34.478
[tense music playing]

38:35.646 --> 38:36.814
Who sent you?

38:38.065 --> 38:39.734
Who sent you? [groans]

38:41.360 --> 38:42.403
[Mr. Choi groaning]

38:47.283 --> 38:48.951
[both grunting]

38:52.204 --> 38:53.539
[groans]

38:55.708 --> 38:57.126
[grunts]

38:59.962 --> 39:01.255
Fuck.

39:03.674 --> 39:04.759
[both grunting]

39:09.889 --> 39:11.182
[groaning]

39:17.772 --> 39:19.357
[both grunting]

39:23.944 --> 39:25.196
[Myeong-gil groaning]

39:32.161 --> 39:34.455
- [Myeong-gil grunts]
- [groans]

39:46.967 --> 39:48.594
[Mr. Choi grunting]

39:58.604 --> 40:01.273
[grunting]

40:02.566 --> 40:05.861
[screaming]

40:16.080 --> 40:16.997
[both grunting]

40:26.340 --> 40:27.508
[shouting]

40:31.846 --> 40:33.431
- [In-beom grunts]
- [Mr. Choi groans]

40:34.056 --> 40:35.349
Sir, are you okay?

40:35.433 --> 40:36.684
Kill that fucker!

40:40.187 --> 40:41.439
[In-beom grunting]

40:47.736 --> 40:49.780
[In-beom shouting]

40:57.037 --> 40:58.247
[ominous music playing]

41:00.499 --> 41:02.501
[shallow breathing]

41:09.675 --> 41:10.759
[In-beom whimpers]

41:14.680 --> 41:15.681
[exhales]

41:25.691 --> 41:27.067
It's okay, Beom. Huh?

41:27.151 --> 41:29.153
- Snap out of it. You're okay.
- Okay.

41:29.236 --> 41:30.488
Yes, sir.

41:30.571 --> 41:32.114
- Kang In-beom!
- Yes, sir!

41:34.033 --> 41:35.159
We don't have time.

41:35.784 --> 41:38.204
Take all the money in the safe
and head down first, okay?

41:38.287 --> 41:39.622
[panting]

41:40.539 --> 41:41.916
[Myeong-gil exhales deeply]

41:43.042 --> 41:45.127
Calm down. Calm down.

41:45.794 --> 41:47.379
[tense music playing]

42:06.732 --> 42:08.108
[panting]

42:15.658 --> 42:16.575
Huh?

42:17.243 --> 42:18.202
Sir!

42:19.453 --> 42:20.788
He's not there!

42:22.122 --> 42:23.332
[exhales deeply]

42:25.960 --> 42:27.461
- Just go downstairs.
- Yes, sir.

42:31.131 --> 42:32.424
[panting]

42:37.471 --> 42:39.014
[dramatic music building]

42:48.107 --> 42:49.149
[music ends]

42:49.233 --> 42:50.901
- [Mr. Oh] Mr. Choi.
- Hm?

42:51.902 --> 42:53.195
[grunts, exhales]

43:10.754 --> 43:12.089
[Mr. Choi grunting]

43:20.848 --> 43:22.600
Have you thought about it yet?

43:26.895 --> 43:28.314
What's the problem?

43:29.648 --> 43:31.191
Let's avoid Yang Jae-myeong.

43:32.109 --> 43:32.943
Why?

43:33.652 --> 43:35.613
Those people also resort to killing.

43:35.696 --> 43:37.573
I want to move the bookstore as well.

43:37.656 --> 43:39.199
[scoffs] Why?

43:39.283 --> 43:40.242
Hyeon-ju.

43:43.621 --> 43:44.455
Look at me.

43:46.373 --> 43:47.791
[gentle piano music playing]

43:48.584 --> 43:50.544
I am old and tired.

43:51.128 --> 43:53.339
There's no strength or courage left in me

43:54.590 --> 43:55.674
to fight them.

43:56.175 --> 43:58.802
I just want to live
my remaining days in peace,

43:59.470 --> 44:01.639
teaching you the things
I want to teach you,

44:02.723 --> 44:04.475
and giving you all the things that…

44:06.518 --> 44:09.188
that I want to leave to you
once I'm not here anymore.

44:11.106 --> 44:13.108
That is the only thing I want right now.

44:18.030 --> 44:19.865
Do you understand what I'm saying?

44:25.537 --> 44:26.622
Good.

44:27.998 --> 44:29.041
And thank you.

44:34.380 --> 44:35.756
[suspenseful music playing]

44:47.267 --> 44:48.268
[lock beeping]

44:59.905 --> 45:00.739
[lock beeps]

45:19.216 --> 45:20.968
[engine revs]

45:21.051 --> 45:22.177
[music builds]

45:44.491 --> 45:45.492
[music fades]

45:50.164 --> 45:51.290
[tense music playing]

45:52.291 --> 45:54.126
Remember, the value of gold rises

45:54.668 --> 45:58.797
every single time people lose confidence
in fiat currency.

45:59.506 --> 46:01.216
You gotta your slush fund in gold.

46:01.967 --> 46:05.429
Besides, if you melt the gold down
and mix it with other gold,

46:05.512 --> 46:06.597
it launders itself.

46:07.890 --> 46:10.309
That was the very first thing I learned
when I worked for Choi.

46:14.313 --> 46:16.482
Failing to get my hands
on his hidden gold…

46:18.942 --> 46:20.778
is something that I still regret.

46:21.487 --> 46:23.030
That old stupid fuck.

46:24.198 --> 46:27.576
He suddenly grows a conscience
and closes down the damn company.

46:29.119 --> 46:29.953
[In-beom grunts]

46:32.623 --> 46:33.916
[In-beom gasps]

46:35.918 --> 46:37.002
[In-beom exhales]

46:48.055 --> 46:51.600
[keypad beeping]

47:13.247 --> 47:14.122
[chuckles]

47:20.045 --> 47:22.130
- Beom.
- Yes, sir.

47:22.923 --> 47:24.049
[Myeong-gil] Get in here.

47:35.394 --> 47:36.353
What do you think?

47:36.895 --> 47:38.480
It's amazing.

47:40.816 --> 47:41.692
[chuckles]

47:43.652 --> 47:45.612
[Myeong-gil]
Each bar is worth 500 million.

47:45.696 --> 47:47.531
If our business in Korea goes south,

47:48.824 --> 47:51.702
you and I will take all this gold
and go to Vietnam.

47:51.785 --> 47:52.828
Huh?

47:52.911 --> 47:53.996
We can hide there.

47:54.079 --> 47:56.582
I planted someone
in the Vietnamese government.

47:57.958 --> 47:58.792
Thanks to this,

48:00.419 --> 48:03.422
we should be able to live like kings
for the rest of our days.

48:03.505 --> 48:04.464
[In-beom gasps]

48:05.757 --> 48:06.717
Thank you, sir. I…

48:09.595 --> 48:10.554
[chuckles]

48:11.680 --> 48:13.473
You're a brother to me.

48:14.057 --> 48:15.684
I would do anything for you.

48:17.436 --> 48:18.270
Beom, listen.

48:20.814 --> 48:23.901
Out here, you are all I've got.

48:25.485 --> 48:26.570
You know that, right?

48:27.613 --> 48:28.488
Mm-hm.

48:30.115 --> 48:30.949
[chuckles]

48:34.077 --> 48:36.371
[Woo-jin] Come on. [exhales deeply]

48:36.455 --> 48:38.749
[Gun-woo] It's the best
stir-fried spicy pork in the world.

48:38.832 --> 48:40.500
- [Hyeon-ju] It's that good?
- Yeah.

48:42.210 --> 48:44.379
[woman crying]

48:50.177 --> 48:51.929
Auntie? Auntie!

48:52.012 --> 48:53.221
[screams]

48:53.305 --> 48:55.766
- Auntie. Auntie.
- [crying]

48:56.308 --> 48:58.143
It's okay. It's okay. It's me, Woo-jin.

48:58.226 --> 49:01.271
[sobbing] Oh God, Woo-jin.
Woo-jin, Woo-jin.

49:02.022 --> 49:03.273
[Woo-jin] What happened?

49:04.149 --> 49:06.735
[owner] I… I took out a private loan.

49:07.444 --> 49:08.946
They told me to pay them back.

49:09.029 --> 49:12.491
I told them I had no money
because I didn't get any customers today.

49:12.574 --> 49:14.952
And they smashed everything.

49:15.035 --> 49:17.663
God, I'm scared. I'm so scared.

49:18.956 --> 49:20.540
What do I do?

49:21.083 --> 49:22.459
[crying continues]

49:26.338 --> 49:29.174
[Woo-jin] How is she supposed to
operate her business if you smash it up?

49:29.257 --> 49:31.051
How do you expect her to pay you back now?

49:31.551 --> 49:33.303
[loan shark] She wasn't paying.
What should I do?

49:33.387 --> 49:35.681
You should ease up on them.
Everyone's having a tough time.

49:35.764 --> 49:37.724
And how am I supposed to make a living?

49:37.808 --> 49:39.893
You know what, why don't you pay for her?

49:40.477 --> 49:43.480
[sighs] Come on,
you know I don't have the money for that.

49:43.563 --> 49:45.190
Then just shut your goddamn mouth.

49:45.273 --> 49:47.067
And mind your own fucking business.

49:47.859 --> 49:49.695
- Got it?
- Fine.

49:54.700 --> 49:55.617
[sighs]

49:59.329 --> 50:00.205
It's Im.

50:01.623 --> 50:03.125
I worked with him back in the day.

50:03.208 --> 50:06.086
Apparently, he just got conned
by someone he lent 500 million to.

50:06.169 --> 50:08.005
- Is Yang Jae-myeong involved?
- [Woo-jin] I don't know.

50:08.088 --> 50:10.215
I didn't ask for the details.

50:10.298 --> 50:13.510
But it was a homeless person's ID
that they used to open a fake account.

50:13.593 --> 50:14.511
Identical MO.

50:15.095 --> 50:16.054
It's him.

50:17.389 --> 50:18.390
I say we should catch him.

50:20.600 --> 50:22.519
I can't just stand by
and do nothing about it.

50:23.103 --> 50:24.938
[sighs] Grandpa told us to lie low.

50:25.814 --> 50:27.190
That they're really dangerous.

50:27.274 --> 50:29.526
But I think it's wrong to do nothing
after seeing all that.

50:30.110 --> 50:32.446
What if I call him back
and tip him off about Yang Jae-myeong,

50:32.529 --> 50:33.613
so he can catch him himself.

50:34.740 --> 50:36.867
If the goal is to capture him,
we should do it.

50:37.367 --> 50:38.577
Maybe we could make some money.

50:38.660 --> 50:42.289
If we do make money from this,
can I use it to help out Auntie?

50:42.372 --> 50:45.375
If we do, we'll split it evenly.
Feel free to use it however you see fit.

50:46.626 --> 50:49.254
- Cool.
- Then I want to help her too.

50:49.838 --> 50:50.672
[exhales]

50:53.091 --> 50:54.009
Come here.

50:57.763 --> 50:59.514
- Come on over.
- No. [groans]

51:00.724 --> 51:01.641
[Gun-woo chuckles]

51:02.642 --> 51:03.560
Thank you.

51:06.813 --> 51:08.356
[tense music playing]

51:14.404 --> 51:15.655
[engine revs]

51:18.033 --> 51:18.867
All in.

51:32.005 --> 51:34.424
[man] Sir, you should look at this.

51:36.968 --> 51:38.386
That car over there.

51:39.513 --> 51:41.890
They cut the engine,
but no one's getting out.

51:44.810 --> 51:46.144
- Hey, get ready.
- Yes, sir.

51:47.437 --> 51:48.855
Hey, check your phone.

51:48.939 --> 51:50.065
- Yes, sir.
- Okay, okay.

51:56.822 --> 51:58.198
Hey, sir, they're here.

51:58.698 --> 52:02.035
[Jun-min sighs]
In exactly two hours, make your move.

52:02.119 --> 52:03.662
[tense music continues]

52:14.506 --> 52:15.340
[sighs]

52:26.101 --> 52:27.102
They're here.

52:35.527 --> 52:36.486
Let's go. Let's go.

52:42.534 --> 52:44.578
You're gonna die today, you dumb fucks.

52:51.001 --> 52:52.794
- [Hyeon-ju inhales sharply]
- [car starts]

52:59.509 --> 53:00.844
[engine revs]

53:00.927 --> 53:01.845
[music building]

53:27.829 --> 53:28.955
[music ends]

53:30.665 --> 53:32.375
[laughing]

53:33.460 --> 53:35.003
[ominous music playing]

53:50.268 --> 53:51.144
Yes, sir.

53:52.187 --> 53:53.313
Come down now.

53:54.481 --> 53:56.316
[both breathing heavily]

53:56.399 --> 53:57.776
[suspenseful music playing]

54:03.448 --> 54:04.532
Come out!

54:05.450 --> 54:08.954
Hey, you fuckers, I know you're there,
so hurry up and show yourselves.

54:09.037 --> 54:11.790
Come out, assholes!
What is this, hide-and-seek?

54:12.624 --> 54:13.500
Motherfuckers.

54:21.216 --> 54:22.425
[gasps]

54:27.764 --> 54:28.598
Please pick up…

54:29.391 --> 54:30.225
Please.

54:30.308 --> 54:32.185
HYEON-JU

54:33.061 --> 54:33.895
[grunts]

54:37.274 --> 54:38.566
- Mm?
- [Hyeon-ju] Grandpa.

54:38.650 --> 54:40.026
Woo-jin and Gun-woo are in danger.

54:41.111 --> 54:42.195
Where are you?

54:42.279 --> 54:44.489
- [goon 1] Get a move on.
- [goon 2] Let's go! Let's go!

54:44.572 --> 54:45.991
[goon 1] You sons of bitches!

54:46.074 --> 54:48.243
- [goon 3] Let's get 'em.
- [Woo-jin] Fuck.

54:48.326 --> 54:49.160
[Woo-jin gasps]

54:49.661 --> 54:52.038
- [goon 1] Get a move on.
- [Woo-jin] Go, go, go!

54:53.498 --> 54:55.917
Oh, fuck. This is insane.

54:57.460 --> 54:59.004
[goon 1] Hey, you sons of bitches.

55:00.005 --> 55:01.298
[metal clanking]

55:08.805 --> 55:10.098
[music builds, ends]

55:10.181 --> 55:11.266
[theme music playing]

57:00.375 --> 57:01.418
[theme music ends]
